# botv2 environment template.
#   • Local:  copy to  botv2/.env  and fill in (that file is gitignored).
#   • Prod:   set these as Railway service variables (NOT in a file).
# Values here are placeholders / safe defaults — never commit real secrets.

# ── REQUIRED ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# v2's OWN Discord bot token — a DIFFERENT bot application than v1.
DISCORD_TOKEN=
# Kevin's Discord user id (numeric) — used for DMs + in-flight ticket detection.
KEVIN_USER_ID=
# Shared secret for the x-bot-key header on the portal's /bot/price.
# Must equal the value the portal expects. This is NOT the Triumph token.
BOT_API_KEY=
# Google service-account credentials as inline JSON (the whole object on one line).
# This is the prod/Railway path. (Locally you may instead set GOOGLE_CREDENTIALS_FILE.)
GOOGLE_CREDENTIALS_JSON=

# ── IMPORTANT IN PROD ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Point at a MOUNTED VOLUME so ticket / owed / tracking state survives redeploys.
# Without a volume the container is ephemeral and this is wiped on every deploy.
DATA_DIR=/data
# v2's OWN Google Drive folder id for buying sheets. MUST differ from v1's folder
# while both bots run, or v1's folder-wide sweeps ingest v2's sheets (see DEPLOY.md
# isolation note #1). Share the new folder with the same service-account email.
# If this is left unset, v2 REFUSES to create buying sheets (tripwire) rather than
# writing into v1's folder — quoting still works, sheets are disabled until you set it.
PSA_FOLDER_ID=
# Escape hatch: set to 1 ONLY to intentionally share v1's folder (safe only once v1
# is retired). Leave blank for the normal "v2 has its own folder" path.
ALLOW_SHARED_PSA_FOLDER=

# ── OPTIONAL (config.py has working defaults; override only to change them) ────
# PORTAL_BASE_URL=https://portal.ktscollectibles.com
# GOOGLE_CREDENTIALS_FILE=~/Downloads/google_credentials.json   # local alt to _JSON
# APPS_SCRIPT_URL=            # defaults to the live buying-sheet Apps Script
# TEMPLATE_SHEET_ID=         # defaults to the "Buying Form KTS Collectibles" template
# SPORTS_OP_MIN_LOT=1500
# POKEMON_SINGLES_MIN_LOT=1500
# MIN_LOT_VALUE=0            # combined-lot minimum (0 = off)
# MIN_SLAB_COUNT=0           # slab-count minimum (0 = off)
# POKEMON_LANE_OPEN=        # set to 1 when the Pokémon (Pixel) lane opens
# BOTV2_PRICE_MOCK=         # set to 1 to answer with MOCK prices (offline testing)
# PORT is injected by Railway automatically — do NOT set it yourself.
